  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Honest notes",
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "\n- **Sharing result:** at the same traffic per model, GPU busy went from 38% (one copy alone) to 93% (six sharing) and mean answer time from 81 ms to 396 ms. GPU busy is DCGM utilization, not useful work: at saturation one copy alone delivers about the same total requests per second as six sharing (40.5 vs 41.9), so sharing adds room for several models, not throughput.\n- **Heavy load result:** six copies delivered about 5x less total throughput than one copy, because one tiny server already fills the card. Sharing helps when many models each get light traffic, not when one model is saturated.\n- **Equal speed:** utilization, throughput and training time did not differ between the two paths. Do not read the first-time setup bar as a Kubernetes win: it is the one-time cost.\n- **Recovery times** are from pod logs and polling (about +/- 3 s). Not tested: Growing, Moving, MIG, the Operator installing the driver or toolkit.\n- Source: `results-ubuntu-4070.md` in the repo, branch `ubuntu-4070`.\n"
   },
